This letter attests that the security finding described below, identified in a penetration test conducted on 2025-05-16, has been remediated in the Normain production environment.

## Finding

* **Severity:** Medium

* **Classification:** OWASP A5/A6 — Security Misconfiguration

* **Host:** <https://app.normain.com/> (port 443/tcp)

* **Description:** Server responded with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *` to requests containing a `null` Origin header, permitting Cross-Origin Resource Sharing from arbitrary origins.

## Remediation

The CORS policy in the API server (`src/apps/server/api/src/server.ts`) was updated to replace the reflective `origin: true` configuration with an explicit allowlist of trusted tenant origins derived from per-tenant configuration.

* **Commit:** `d2c400e0009e50faf83336a54bbab80ecee5510d`

* **Merged:** 2026-04-23

* **Deployed to production:** \[YYYY-MM-DD]

## Verification

Post-deployment verification confirms the server no longer reflects arbitrary origins:

```
$ curl -I -H "Origin: https://evil.example" https://app.normain.com/
HTTP/2 200
[paste relevant response headers here — confirm no Access-Control-Allow-Origin echoing the injected origin]
```

No `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` is set on the endpoint, further limiting exposure.

